🐭
"Catch"/en"接住"/zh-CN"接住"/zh-TW
=== start/en
¶Catch the scurrying mouse with a click — click again to set it free.

Both sounds come from the poses themselves. A @Pose can carry a @Music, which
plays the moment that pose is struck: the pounce sounds when the mouse's resting
pose changes to the caught one, and the scurry sounds when the spin reaches the
halfway pose it's keyed to. Nothing has to be wired up between the animation and
the sound — the pose is where they meet.¶

¶Two brief pieces. A @Track loops by default, but a pose is an instant rather
than something that lasts, so a pose's music always plays through just once.¶
pounce: 🎼(🎶([5 1] instrument: 🔈.🔔 beat: 1beats) volume: 50% name: 'pounce')
scurry: 🎼(🎶([1 2] instrument: 🔈.🪈 beat: 1beats) volume: 35% name: 'scurry')

¶If the selected phrase is mouse, toggle whether the mouse is caught.¶
name: Choice()
caught: ⊥ … ∆ (name) … (name = 'mouse') & ~caught
¶Every second, move the mouse¶
place:  Place(0m 0m 0m) … ∆ Time(1000ms) … caught ? Place(0m 0m) Place(Random(-2m 2m) Random(-2m 2m))

Stage([
		💬(
			"🐭" 
			selectable: ⊤
			place: place
			resting: caught ? Pose(rotation: 180° music: pounce) Pose()
			moving:caught ? Pose() Sequence({0%: Pose(rotation: 0°) 50%: Pose(rotation: 180° music: scurry) 100%:Pose(rotation: 360°)})
			duration: 1s
			name: 'mouse'
		)
	] 
	place: Place(0m 0m -5m)
	frame: Rectangle(-3m 3m 3m -3m)
)